.TH umount 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
umount \- unmount a filesystem
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B umount
.I device
|
.I directory
.br
.B umount \-a
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B umount
detaches a filesystem.  It may be named either by its device or by the
directory it is mounted on;
.B umount
looks the other up in
.BR /etc/mtab .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a
Unmount everything in
.BR /etc/mtab ,
except the root.
.SH NOTES
A filesystem cannot be unmounted while any process has a file open on it
or has its working directory there.  The usual answer to
.RB `` "device busy" ''
is a shell sitting in that directory:
.B cd /
first.
.PP
Unmounting flushes the buffers for that filesystem, so it is what makes
the card safe to remove.  For the root, which cannot be unmounted, use
.BR remount (1)
to make it read-only instead.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mount (1),
.BR remount (1),
.BR sync (1),
.BR shutdown (1)
